Sval: General's default-browser section holds Startup's settings

Settings' General shows Firefox's default-browser group and, right under it,
Firefox's Startup group, whose one setting Sval shows is the check for the
default browser at launch: two sections about one thing. General's
default-browser group takes the Startup group's items, which also carry
Windows' launch at login, and General does not list the Startup group.
Startup's restore choice stays hidden by its own setting, because Sval's
workspaces decide what a launch reopens (Sval spec §10.4). The group's config
is built in Firefox's file, so no added file can change it.

diff --git a/browser/components/preferences/config/account-sync.mjs b/browser/components/preferences/config/account-sync.mjs
index c0f096e1af..8a03f2679e 100644
--- a/browser/components/preferences/config/account-sync.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/preferences/config/account-sync.mjs
@@ -820,11 +820,14 @@ Preferences.addSetting({
 let accountsEnabled = Services.prefs.getBoolPref("identity.fxaccounts.enabled");
 
 SettingGroupManager.registerGroups({
-  defaultBrowserSync: window.createDefaultBrowserConfig({
-    includeIsDefaultPane: false,
-    inProgress: true,
-    hiddenFromSearch: true,
-  }),
+  // Sval: General's one default-browser section, so it holds the items of
+  // Firefox's Startup group: the check for the default at launch and, on
+  // Windows, the launch at login. Startup's restore choice is hidden in Sval
+  // by its own setting.
+  defaultBrowserSync: (config => ({
+    ...config,
+    items: [...config.items, ...window.createStartupConfig().items],
+  }))(window.createDefaultBrowserConfig({ inProgress: true })),
   accountDisabled: {
     inProgress: true,
     hidden: accountsEnabled,
